Z||000001||theogre||07-13-2001||11:39 PM||||Well... If Canada is anything like down here in this, and I be suprised if they aint...<P>You get caught without it all hell will likely break loose. Potentially the RCMP could probably arrest you on the spot. You might just get a ticket. Allot of it depends on just what kind of mood the Mounty is in...||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||07-14-2001||01:14 AM||||Its generally a bad idea to drive without a liscense. For starters, suppose you get in an accident you have NO insurance whatsoever. You could also get sued bigtime if you were at fault in an accident. I forgot to renew my license last summer (drove almost two weeks without realizing that it had expired, still kicking myself), and when I got pulled over at a routine checkstop I had my car impounded and was given a fairly pricey ticket for driving with an invalid license. Its not worth the risk man, wait a couple weeks and retake your test.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||07-14-2001||02:20 AM||||You will get a fine (Max $5000 I think) and you won't be able to drive for a few years. I don't know why all these Americans think the RCMP will be after you (When I posted a question about de-activating braking systems, someone mentioned the RCMP?) I don't know what you have been reading, but the RCMP doesn't have anything to do with it. OPP maybe..? Mounties? I think it's this whole "Canadians live in Igloos" thing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||07-14-2001||12:26 PM||||big fine for driving without a license<BR>big fine for driving without insurance<BR>you get your G1 license revoked for 2 years I think<BR>you have no insurance, and if you're under 18.. if you get sued because of an accident, your parents will be responsible for the money... (I know a guy who's parents were sued for $150,000 cause of something the kid did.. don't think it couldn't happen.) but if you're 18+.... then YOU are responsible. what happens if you get sued for a half million dollars?<P>best option? just take the test again, as soon as you can..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||07-14-2001||12:27 PM||||Oh yeah, another thing.. a guy I went to school with was caught doing 120 in an 80 zone, by himself, and he only had his G1.. his license was suspended for 2 years.<P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||07-14-2001||12:41 PM||||What's a G2? G1? Some sort of license?<P>Down here, we refer to anything canadian gov't related as: "royal canadian mounted" and then add the division: mounties, queens flying aces, etc...<P>Igloos, with no running water, elec, and only the only paved road is the queens nat'l highway or whatever its called.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||07-14-2001||02:05 PM||||*SIGH*<P>First of all, The RCMP are the national cops<BR>Igloos are only in winter,<BR>No running water 'cos we either sell it to the US, or it's in Housing, <BR>and the Queen's Highway is the shoulder  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000008||grinthock||07-14-2001||02:46 PM||||OK, it's a $5000 MAX FINE as previously stated<P>For our americans<P>G1 - a 5 year learners permit (which our topic poster has) which requires a licensed driver in the car and you can NOT use the freeways, you must REMAIN a G1 for a minimum 8 months before going for a G1-Exit test and enter the G2 program after a 20 minutes road test<P>G2 - a 5 year Graduated parole style license, you have reduced "chances" when it comes to tickets and the like, you can get out of this after 12 months minumum in this program then you need a G2-exit test, it's a 45 Minute driving test in city and on freeway and there is a %40 FAILURE RATE on the first try!<P><BR>If you get caught driving with a G1 here is what happens, and I know, because I have seen it happen to people (not me)<P>1)  The car will be IMPOUNDED, the police impound usually charges $150-$250 to get your car out, PLUS the tow fee, which is usually $40 plus distance<P>2)  Your license at a G-1 level COULD be revoked at the officers discretion<P>3)  You will see a fine of a minimum of $1000 to a max of $5000, 2 people I know got $2500 fines.<P>4)  Your insurance based on the Canadian system will SKYROCKET!  You were charged with Driving without a license, that's the charge.  That puts you into the Canadian Facility Insurnace system, which means that no matter which Insurance company you talk to they will give you the "legislated rate for high risk drivers" which will put your insurance as a 16 yearold to approx $300 / month ($200-300 depending on various factors)<P>Your insurance will be at LEAST $170 per month from 18-21 then $120 / month until you are $25, and ALL THIS assumes you NEVER get another ticket!  Of course all this has various factors that could change the $$$ but this is basically right.... Oh and if you decide you can't afford your Fiero to drive even a cheap POS Hyundai Pony will cost you $120 a month because you are a bad driver.<P>Bottom Line --- HAVE PATIENCE.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrgone||07-14-2001||08:39 PM||||thats not for all of canada there.<P>nova scotia has a completely different licencing system but we use the same names <BR>G1 G2 etc.<P>i never had to do my final driving test because i had my nova scotia G||||reg||1
